    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_three_way_merge_resolver" kindref="compound">ThreeWayMergeResolver</ref></para>
<para>Resolves conflicts by performing a three-way JSON merge.</para>
<para>Algorithm:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Identify the common ancestor write by comparing vector clocks: the write whose clock is dominated by all others is the base. If no unambiguous ancestor exists the write with the smallest HLC timestamp is used as the base.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>For each top-level JSON key in the conflicting writes:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>If only one side changed the key → take that side&apos;s value.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If both sides changed the key → Last-Write-Wins on that key.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If neither side changed the key → take the base value.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Keys present in only one side are included (UNION behaviour).</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Complexity: O(N · F) where N = writes, F = average top-level field count. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
